extraction_notes: |
  Read from Rifts World Book 8: Japan printed 211-212 via the text layer at
  .cache/books/japan (page_offset +1: printed 211 is cache p212, printed 212 is
  cache p213). The lore opens under Japanese Dragons at the foot of printed 211;
  the stat block is printed 212, which was rendered (pymupdf index 212) to read
  every digit-cipher figure: M.D.C. 1D4x100+50 hatchling, 1D4x1000+800 young
  adult, 2D4x1000+200 mature adult; P.P.E. 1D4x100 hatchling, 1D6x100+150 young
  adult, 2D4x100+300 mature adult; I.S.P. 3D6x10; bio-regeneration 1D4x10.

  THE SHAPE IS THE RUE HATCHLINGS''. The species tag line says a player
  character uses the Rifts RPG hatchling R.C.C., and Rifts Ultimate Edition
  printed 158 says the other species use that Dragon R.C.C. for skills and level
  advancement and names this book among them. So this copies
  dragon-hatchling-flame-wind line for line wherever the rule is the common
  R.C.C.''s: the three instinctive skills at 98%, the Special Areas of Interest as
  the related allowance, the secondary skills and their schedule, spells_starting
  0 with the learning ladder as prose, the magic-understanding, size, food,
  cybernetics, money and weapons paragraphs. The species half is this book''s.

  1. HATCHLING FIGURES WHERE THE BOOK PRINTS THEM. M.D.C. and P.P.E. are the
     hatchling''s figures; attacks are "half if a hatchling" of eight, so
     attacks_base 4. The young and mature adult figures are prose. The book
     prints NO +10 M.D.C. per level and no per-level P.P.E. for these species,
     so none is stored; and no hit points, S.D.C. or A.R. for S.D.C. worlds.
  2. ONE FIGURE FOR EVERY AGE. Attributes, horror factor, I.S.P., psionic
     powers, natural abilities, damage and bonuses are printed once, not split by
     age, and are stored as printed. RUE printed 158 converts a hatchling to an
     adult by raising attributes, doubling bonuses and I.S.P.; nothing converts
     the other way, and reversing dice would be invention, not transcription.
     P.S. 2D6+32 is therefore far above any RUE hatchling. Flagged for Nate.
  3. BONUSES: "+2 on all saving throws" is written out across the fourteen d20
     saves, as fire-dragon does; the +8 vs horror factor is its own key.
     coma_death_pct is a percentage and is left out. No pull punch is printed.
  4. PSIONICS: a fixed list of eight, granted by name. Type master because
     the list includes two Super powers (Hypnotic Suggestion, Mind Block
     Auto-Defense); the book states no tier - a judgement. "Automatic mind block
     defense" is the catalog''s Mind Block Auto-Defense.
  5. MAGIC: the species'' spell lists are the grown dragon''s and are a special
     ability; the magic block is the hatchling R.C.C.''s (no spells at level one).
     The Magic line''s own "P.P.E. is 2D4x100" is the adult figure.
  6. SKILLS: the species'' R.C.C. skill list (Japanese, Gobblely, Bonsai, Go and
     the rest) is prose, because RUE printed 158 gives a hatchling species the
     Dragon R.C.C.''s skills. Nothing from it is granted.
  7. MYSTIC MARTIAL ARTS: the species knows all of them and cannot use any, so
     there is no pick to model; it is a special ability. Compare BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md
     F116 for the classes that do pick them.
  8. xp_table: none printed for dragons on the Experience Point Tables (cache
     p217, folio 216; read off a render, no dragon column). Copied from the
     seven dragon-hatchling classes: RUE''s Dragon Hatchling & Adult Dragon ladder,
     RUE printed 295, via ~006-rue-xp-ladders.sql.
  9. horror_factor is a top-level key here where flame-wind has only prose,
     because the Japan entry prints one figure and the key is modelled.
