## Lore

The name means "hideous sorcery serpent", and it fits. The shikome kido-mi is
a sinister dragon that enjoys tormenting and manipulating mortals for its own
gain or simply for the pleasure of it, dangling the promise of mystic power and
arcane knowledge before humans in order to corrupt and control them. It is a
powerful sorcerer, and though it cannot use the mystic martial arts itself it
knows them all, and teaches them to minions who earn the secrets through dark
deeds done for the dragon. Some legends claim the ninja clans learned their arts
of invisibility from one of these dragons.

Too greedy, arrogant and self-driven to work with other powerful beings unless
it serves some hidden purpose, it acknowledges no being - man, dragon or god -
as its better. It has accomplices at best, and more often minions, servants,
slaves and lackeys: oni, wizards, ninja and others.

**Habitat:** Indigenous to an alien dimension; occasionally found anywhere, but
favours Japan, Korea, China, India and Indonesia. Many keep mountain retreats;
some rule villages or even cities from a castle, like a king.

**Enemies:** Everyone, other shikome kido-mi and gods included, is a rival and a
potential enemy. The demon queller counts this dragon among the demons to
destroy.

**Average Life Span:** 8,000 years.

## GM Notes

Average NPC level: 1D4+3 for hatchlings and young adults, 2D4+5 for mature
adults. A player character starts as a first level hatchling.

Grown dragon figures: M.D.C. 1D4x1000+800 (young adult), 2D4x1000+200 (mature
adult); P.P.E. 1D6x100+150 (young adult), 2D4x100+300 (mature adult); six
attacks per melee for a young adult and eight for a mature adult, or two by
magic. Full length 42 feet (12.8 m), one to three tons.

A hatchling of this species is a natural villain''s apprentice and a natural
villain: it knows every mystic martial art and can use none, which makes it a
teacher looking for students and a patron looking for servants.
